+## Two Neon projects
+
+| Project                | Holds                                  |
+| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
+| `project-name`         | production, on its default branch      |
+| `project-name-staging` | `staging` and every `preview/*` branch |
+
+Each has its own project-scoped API key, pinned to its project (`NEON_API_KEY` /
+`NEON_PROJECT_ID`). `.github/actions/neon-env` refuses the other target's project
+(`refuse-project`) before it touches a branch. The Workers connect as `project_name_app`, never
+as the owner ([database.md](database.md#neon)); its password is the `DB_APP_PASSWORD` secret, a
+different one on each side.
+
+When the production account has a Hyperdrive config named `project-name-prod`,
+`prod-deploy.yml` binds it and the Workers connect through it with node-postgres; its caching
+is off, since the app reads its own writes. Without one they connect to Neon directly.
+
